think Lindy-first crux-first: cluster_adjacency reads a cluster PAIR. The prior log named the crux-first next itself -- fold cluster_distance into a whole cluster-neighbor graph. This is to cluster_adjacency exactly what scene_graph is to object_relation: JOIN the pair read over every cluster pair into one matrix, then read the whole-graph questions no pair holds. The cleanest lift, a Lindy-durable layout-grouping primitive.
think Reused the same three-cluster scene cluster_adjacency proves (distances 2, 3, 10; frame overlaps only for clusters 1-2), so the two graphs' edge counts are hand-known before the witness runs. Chose threshold reads (clusters_within, cluster_degree_within) and two edge counts (within_edges, frame_overlap_edges) as the OWNED whole-graph reads -- nearest stays owned by cluster_adjacency, honoring compose-not-braid.
think Built image/cluster_graph.rye modeled on scene_graph.rye's matrix build: build_cluster_graph joins cluster_adjacency over every ordered cluster pair (diagonal a defined placeholder), graph_distance/graph_frames_overlap read the matrix, clusters_within/cluster_degree_within the thresholded neighbors, within_edges/frame_overlap_edges the two graphs' edge counts. Every fn >= 2 positive invariants, cluster count bounded by scene_graph_max_objects, named errors BadClusterId/NoClusters/TooManyClusters.
obs The crux: the frame-overlap graph and the true-distance graph are DIFFERENT graphs, neither a subset of the other, in both directions. At threshold 1 the frame graph holds edge 1-2 the true graph refuses (the floor is 2 -- frame overlap OVER-claims a contact past the threshold); at threshold 3 the true graph holds edge 1-3 (gap 3, disjoint frames) the frame graph MISSES (frame overlap UNDER-claims a real nearness). So a box comparison over frames only BOUNDS the true adjacency graph, never determines it -- the box-is-a-prefilter lesson lifted to the whole cluster graph, the highest level the family has reached.
obs Threshold adjacency is a STAR, never a clique, NOT transitive: cluster 1 lies within 3 of both clusters 2 (gap 2) and 3 (gap 3), yet clusters 2 and 3 stand 10 apart, so cluster 1 is a hub of degree 2 while each other is degree 1 -- the same non-transitivity overlap_degree found at the object level, now tunable by a threshold at the cluster level.
obs GREEN on the FIRST full metal run, no reds. Learned from the prior lap's two compound asserts -- caught two `or` compound invariants (assert(count + 1 <= clusters or clusters == count)) before build and simplified each to a single positive bound (a neighbor count can never reach the cluster count), a clarity fix not an algorithm red, none booked. Live clock 012707 read and stamped exactly, no future stamp (REDS #75's lesson). TAME bans clean, width-check exit 0, living-card ASCII GREEN, plain 7-bit ASCII.
obs Council rota lap deep-read ORGANIZING.md (item 21) -- the placement law: a piece is filed by what it DOES, code implementing a module lives in that module's home (image/), witnesses in tools/, and the reasoning trace here; the live card of what is next stays single-stranded, never a second copy of the log index.
